.\n- **Pass 2** (single-core, 1 tile): reads accumulated S, applies final transform, writes result. For p==1 and p==inf the final transform is identity — pass 2 still runs but just copies, keeping the code path uniform.\n\n## Pinned-v2 APIs\n\n- `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` for 1-D GM views\n- `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [TILE], real_shape=[n])` / `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])`\n- `asc2.range(start, stop, step, unroll_factor=2)` — NO `gm_barrier`, NO `parallel`\n- `asc2.reduce_sum`, `asc2.reduce_max` for tile → scalar\n- `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm, [offset])`, `asc2.atomic_max(src_tile, dst_gm, [offset])`\n- `asc2.full([8], scalar, dtype=asc.float32)` for scalar widening before atomic\n- `asc2.abs`, `asc2.sqrt`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.log` for element-wise\n- `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile_size (compile-time)\n- `.to(asc.float32)` / `.to(x.dtype)` for dtype promotion/cast-back\n- Scalar accumulator seed: `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n\n## All 20 Cases Coverage\n\n| Case | Shapes (nelem) | dtype | p | Special notes |\n|------|---------------|-------|---|--------------|\n| 1 | 2x [1024,1024] ~1M | f16 | 1.0 | L1 path |\n| 2 | 3x [2048,2048] ~4M | f32 | 1.0 | L1 path, no promotion needed |\n| 3 | 1x [4096,4096] ~16M | bf16 | 1.0 | L1 path, large tensor |\n| 4 | 1x [2048,2048] ~4M | f16 | 2.0 | L2 path |\n| 5 | 3x [2048,4096] ~8M | f32 | 3.0 | General path |\n| 6 | 1x [1023,1023] ~1M | bf16 | 1.5 | General path, odd dims |\n| 7 | 1x [1009,1021] ~1M | f16 | 1.5 | General path, non-power-of-2 |\n| 8 | 1x [1537,769] ~1.2M | f32 | 4.0 | General path |\n| 9 | 2x [363,367,373] ~50M | bf16 | 2.0 | L2 path, 3D |\n| 10 | 1x [2049,513] ~1M | f16 | 1.0 | Full f16 range [-65504, 65504] |\n| 11 | 3x [3,7,13,4001] ~1M | f32 | 2.0 | L2 path, 4D |\n| 12 | 1x [1000003] ~1M | bf16 | inf | Inf-norm, values include +/-inf |\n| 13 | 1x [11,13,17,67,67] ~1.7M | f32 | 5.0 | General path, 5D |\n| 14 | 1x [3,7,11,13,1009] ~3M | f16 | 2.0 | **All-zero input** → sum=0, sqrt(0)=0 |\n| 15 | 2x [512,2049] ~1M | f32 | 2.0 | L2 path |\n| 16 | 4x [255,8193] ~2M | bf16 | 1.0 | L1 path, 4 tensors |\n| 17 | 1x [4097,511] ~2M | f16 | -1.0 | Negative p; spec guarantees nonzero elements |\n| 18 | 2x [2,511,2049] ~2M | f32 | 2.0 | L2 path, 3D |\n| 19 | 2x [4,255,2049] ~2M | bf16 | 3.0 | General path, 3D |\n| 20 | 4x [2,3,17,1024,101] ~10.5M | f32 | 2.5 | General path, 5D, large |\n\n## Tiling\n\n- **TILE = 2048** for all paths. Simple paths (p=1,2,inf) could use 4096 but 2048 keeps one kernel specialization and is safe for the general log-exp chain.\n- Tile size is `asc.ConstExpr[int]` — baked at compile time.\n- For small tensors (< TILE), single tile with real_shape handles it.\n- Grid stride: `num_tiles = ceildiv(size, TILE)`, `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`.\n\n## Tails\n\n- `n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off`\n- `real_shape=[n]` on both `copy_in` and `copy_out`\n- No host padding; partial tiles are handled natively via real_shape.\n- All case shapes are non-aligned (e.g., 1009*1021, 1537*769, 1000003) — tails are exercised in nearly every case.\n\n## UB Budget\n\nMeasured calibration: sigmoid chain (6 f32 values, unroll=2, TILE=2048) = 155648 bytes. Factor ≈ 1.6x over naive `visible * 4 * TILE * 2`.\n\n**Pass-1 general kernel** (worst case, p not in {1, 2, inf}):\n- Live f32 tiles: xf (cast), abs(xf), log(|xf|), log(|xf|)*p, exp(log(|xf|)*p) = 5 tiles\n- Naive: 5 * 4 * 2048 * 2 = 81920 bytes\n- Estimated with 1.6x: ~131072 bytes\n- Plus accumulator seed tile + atomic widen tile: +2*4*8 = negligible\n- **Total ~135 KB < 253952 B — FITS**\n\n**Pass-1 simple kernels** (p=1, p=2, p=inf):\n- Live f32 tiles: xf, abs/xf*xf = 2-3 tiles\n- Estimated: ~80-100 KB — comfortable margin\n\n**Pass-2 kernel** (single-core, [8] tile):\n- Trivial: one 8-element tile — negligible UB\n\n**Verdict**: TILE=2048 is safe for all paths. No UB overflow risk.\n\n## Numerical Risks\n\n1. **log(0) = -inf**: For general p path, if element is 0: log(0) = -inf, -inf * p = -inf (p>0) or +inf (p<0), exp(-inf)=0 or exp(+inf)=inf. Case 14 has all zeros with p=2 — but p=2 uses the sqrt(sum(v*v)) path, not general. Safe. No case has zeros with general-p kernel.\n2. **Overflow in exp(log(|v|)*p)**: Max |v| across general cases:\n   - Case 5: |v|≤0.1, p=3 → exp(log(0.1)*3)=exp(-6.9)≈0.001. Safe.\n   - Case 8: |v|≤10, p=4 → exp(log(10)*4)=exp(9.21)≈10000. Sum over 1.2M → ~1.2e10. log(1.2e10)≈23.9, /4=5.98, exp(5.98)≈395. f32 safe.\n   - Case 13: |v|≤10, p=5 → exp(log(10)*5)=exp(11.51)≈100000. Sum over 1.7M → ~1.7e11. log=25.86, /5=5.17, exp(5.17)≈176. Safe.\n   - Case 17: p=-1 → exp(log(|v|)*(-1))=1/|v|. |v|∈(0,1000]. Min nonzero → large but sum is bounded. f32 range sufficient.\n   - Case 19: |v|≤6, p=3 → exp(log(6)*3)=exp(5.37)≈216. Safe.\n   - Case 20: |v|≤40, p=2.5 → exp(log(40)*2.5)=exp(9.22)≈10100. Sum over 10.5M → ~1e11. f32 safe.\n3. **Accumulator overflow (f32)**: Max partial sum per core ≈ total_sum / 72. Worst case: case 9 with p=2, |v|≤100, 50M elements → sum ≈ 50M * 10000 = 5e11. f32 holds ~3.4e38. Safe.\n4. **Catastrophic cancellation**: Not applicable — we use sum of non-negative terms (|v|^p ≥ 0). No subtraction.\n5. **sqrt(0)**: Case 14 all-zeros. sqrt(0)=0. Correct.\n6. **inf inputs (case 12)**: max(|inf|) = inf. IEEE propagation is correct. For bf16, inf is representable.\n7. **f16 precision**: All compute in f32, cast final scalar back to input dtype. Threshold: f16 = 2^-10 ≈ 9.8e-4, bf16 = 2^-7 ≈ 7.8e-3, f32 = 2^-13 ≈ 1.2e-4. f32 accumulation gives ~6-7 digits, well within all thresholds.\n\n## Anti-Cheat Constraints\n\n- ALL math inside `@asc2.jit` kernels\n- torch used ONLY for: `torch.zeros`/`torch.empty` allocation, `.numel()`, `.dtype`, `.device`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`, `.view()`\n- NO `torch.norm`, NO tensor arithmetic on host, NO `.to(dtype)` on device data\n- Host iterates list, launches kernels per tensor, returns list of 0-dim tensors\n- `ensure_npu_platform()` called at top of public function\n- Output is freshly allocated (not views of input)\n\n## Local Validation Ladder\n\n1. **Syntax gate**: `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py`\n2. **Static contract check**: worker harness validates module shape, imports, callable signature\n3. **Exact-v2 compile gate**: `python3 -c \"import candidate\"` with pinned pyasc v2 — all 20 case routes must lower through JIT without compile error\n4. **No numerical verification**: no NPU/camodel available; evidence label is `verified-local-compile` at best\n5. **Submission requires**: camodel for numerical evidence, CANNBench on real NPU for acceptance","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":125,"totalLines":125,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/foreach_norm-generate/design.md","time":{"start":1788349213096,"end":1788349213101}},"id":"prt_061eb675b001wy5qbPEwMul5PT","sessionID":"ses_f9e14bf40ffecLp9VZ81GFZuu1","messageID":"msg_061eb5d7b001UuFgs019Koa5Eq"}}
